WEBVTT

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.080
<b>Shogi Club</b>

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.080
<b>Urushi Yaotome</b>

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.080
<b>Ayumu Tanaka</b>

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.420
It's good to see you, Senpai.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.580
I hope we can...

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.000
H-hey.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.880
Well, shall we get started?

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:34.920
Uh, yeah.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.790
Here's to a good game.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.420
Hello? My hair?

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.080
There is no way he hasn't noticed.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:55.000
Why won't he say anything about it?

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:11.210
Senpai.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.630
Your hair is different than usual. It's cute.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.000
Oh, uh, well, I lost one of my hair ties,
so I had to change it up...

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.330
Thanks for having me!

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.960
Uh, what? Are you gonna challenge us to a duel?

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.330
This is our new ghost club member.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.670
The man, Takeru Kakuryu. Pleasure to meet you!

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.920
An awfully lively ghost...

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.580
Now, let's take one step forward

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.960
Let me feel your heartbeat

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.380
Tactics require a poker face

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.210
Because I don't want my opponent to realize

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.750
For distance, a few centimeters

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.790
Take the long way

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:03.500
Aiming for a smile

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.710
A secret strategy

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.880
An airtight defense

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:13.080
Just a little more

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.500
I'll meet you halfway, so look the other way

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:23.710
I get scared of being hurt

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.750
There are nights like that

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.250
A chance that comes from crossed signals

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.540
I won't let it escape me. I'll turn the tables

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.290
Now, let's take one step forward

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.420
Write your own story

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:50.000
The opening sentence always starts with "actually," "I always"

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.670
The twist is in progressive tense

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.080
Let me feel your heartbeat

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.580
Tactics require a poker face

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.580
Because I don't want my opponent to realize

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.710
Takeru Kakuryu, huh?

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.040
<b>Shogi Club</b>

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.040
<b>Urushi Yaotome</b>

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.040
<b>Ayumu Tanaka</b>

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:12.040
<b>Takeru Kaku</b>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.000
With a name like that, you'd have
to be amazingly good at shogi.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.330
<b>Game 3: I Want to Go on a First Date, Senpai</b>

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.420
You think so?

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.960
Takeru. Have you played shogi before?

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.500
No, I know the rules, and that's it.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.670
Senpai. Would you be so kind as
to play a game with Takeru?

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:25.670
Of course!

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.210
Here's to a good game.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.670
Okay, are you ready to start, Takeru?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.880
When you do it all proper like this,
it kinda gets you weirdly excited, huh?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.210
You think so?

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.130
Oohh, you made a nice sound there.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.790
Senpai, I can make nice sounds, too, you know.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.290
Listen to this. I'll make a much better sound
than anything Takeru can come up with!

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.880
If only this wasn't a portable shogi board!

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.130
You even know the standard moves.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.710
Are you sure you've never done this before?

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.920
No, this is the first time, I promise.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.000
Maybe you have a hidden talent for it.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:12.540
Really?

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:13.630
Really!

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:23.630
Oh, I'm sorry, Ayumu.
You don't get to play because of me.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.210
Don't worry about it. You'll learn more
if you play against Senpai than against me.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.580
Besides, as long as I can see that Senpai is happy,
that's good enough for me.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.250
I wondered... why you weren't coming back to the library.

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.170
No, wait!

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.290
I am a man, and since I joined this club,
as a man, I have to...

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.920
We're going back.

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:01.670
Right away.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.290
Sorry to have bothered you.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.290
What just happened?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.460
Hypnotism.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.080
What!?

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.380
Anyway, Senpai.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.630
Don't you think you gave him a little too much praise?

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.330
What's this, Tanaka? Is this jealousy I'm hearing?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.380
I dunno.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.250
Whoa! That was a conspicuously nice sound!

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.460
<b>Reading Week</b>

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.460
<b>School Library</b>

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:51.170
<b>Check Out / Return</b>

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.290
Why did you do that?

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.880
Because you were intruding.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:57.540
Our Ayumu-kun was so antisocial and all
he ever cared about was kendo. But now he's in love.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.790
I told you to look me in the eye when you talk!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:01.960
I...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:03.830
Can't do that.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.080
Anyway, we should support Ayumu-kun in his love.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:11.170
We shouldn't get in the way.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.420
Support him in his love, eh?

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:15.830
I'll think about it.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.170
Good. I'm glad you understand.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.290
By the way, do you...

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:27.000
Hm?

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:29.290
Do you have anyone, Sakurako?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:32.080
I-I mean, anyone you're in love with?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.830
No, I don't.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.540
Oh. Really.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.210
What was I expecting!?

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.500
What about you?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:45.960
Is there someone you're in love with?

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.210
Yes, and it's you!

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.580
Of course not.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:52.750
Oh really.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.130
Let me know if you find someone.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:56.920
I'll be ready to help you out.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:00.000
My chances... are in the negative...

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.250
I can't anymore. It hurts too much.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.080
Where are you going?

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.630
The john.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.290
And Sakurako, you tell me if you find someone, too.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.710
I'll help you, too.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.330
Thank you!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.500
But I don't think I'm going to be interested
in that kind of thing for a while.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:25.880
Right now, I'm happy just being able
to spend time with you, Takeru-kun.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.380
Oof.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.170
Don't you need to use the restroom?

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.330
I changed my mind.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:42.380
Are you doing that on purpose?

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.040
Doing what?

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.960
No, I mean... sometimes I wonder...

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:51.540
Forget it.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.630
Tell me what you're...

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.380
Seriously, stop that!

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:06.000
He never did come back, did he?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.130
Takeru, I mean.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:12.130
That's a happi, isn't it?

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:14.500
Yup. I'm gonna wear it at the school festival.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.040
Oh yeah, that's just around the corner.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.920
What will your class be doing?

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.580
Selling yakisoba.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.710
The boys are going to do all the setup.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.920
The girls are going to cook on the day of,
and be salesgirls.

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:28.380
I hope you'll come get some!

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.460
Of course I'm going to get some.

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:33.500
This is my senpai's yakisoba.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:35.790
Nothing in this world could keep me away!

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.500
Why are you that enthusiastic!?

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.580
<b>SCHOOL</b>

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.580
<b>FESTIVAL</b>

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.250
What's your class going to do, Tanaka?
Something yummy?

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.830
My class managed to get out of doing a display by
saying something about everyone doing their own thing,

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.000
so... nothing...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.630
Oh. Okay.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.670
I think three balls will be enough.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:01.710
I don't see why not.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.670
Make sure to have lots of prizes to give out.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:05.960
And don't forget the spare targets.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.380
Oh, did I have those?

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.790
Last year, they destroyed the target.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.170
You're not supposed to mention that.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:11.960
I guess the soccer team is doing a target game.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:18.080
What's the matter, Senpai?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:22.920
Nothing. I was just thinking, if we were an official club,
we could have a display, too.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.250
I'm sure we'll be able to do that next year.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.250
Yeah. I hope you're right.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:30.380
Me, too.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.250
We did get Takeru to join, after all.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.130
What?

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.080
Nothing.

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:38.540
Um, Senpai.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.500
Will you walk around the festival with me?

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:52.210
Oh, you mean we can go around the festival
looking for new people to join our club!

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.000
No.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.040
I want to go on a date with you.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:57.420
What!?

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.420
Uh, well...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.540
If you're not comfortable calling it a date,
then we can call it member recruitment.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.540
I just want to be there with you.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:08.460
Is that a no?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.580
Uh, well...

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:14.460
O-okay, I guess I could r...recruit club members with you.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:18.330
And it's not because I'm embarrassed
to call it a date or anything.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.630
It's important to look for people to join the club.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:23.080
I understand. Thank you very much.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.960
I will look forward to our date!

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:26.790
H-hey!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.500
I'm sorry! I meant member recruitment!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.960
<b>SCHOOL</b>

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.960
<b>FESTIVAL</b>

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.290
Yakisoba!

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.710
Yakisoba!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:51.330
Yakisoba! Would you like some yakisoba?

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.210
Yakisoba!

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.170
Nngh, I'm not selling any.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:58.080
But there are so many people here.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.710
One... please...

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.670
Yes, that will be 100 yen!

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:07.750
You're unusually tired.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.080
Yes, Senpai.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:13.790
I went to your class...
and they told me you were out selling...

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.920
So I ran all over campus looking for you.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.210
I want to go on a date with you.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:25.420
Are we... doing club recruitment, then?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:26.500
Yes, Senpai.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:31.130
I'll be free as soon as I sell all these,
so would you mind waiting a bit?

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.540
I'll help you.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.080
I'm good at this kind of thing.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.580
Would anyone like some yakisoba!?

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.580
That was loud.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.630
I had to shout loud in kendo.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.000
One, please.

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:49.000
Thank you very much!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.290
Wow. I already sold one!

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.830
Let's keep it up!

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.630
Yakisoba!

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:58.380
Get your delicious yakisoba, right here!

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.920
Yes, thank you very much!

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.040
It's 100 yen!

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:05.500
Okay, got it!

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.250
Ha ha, thank you so much!

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.830
Yes, we still have some.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.960
Sure, coming right up.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.250
Thank you, thank you, we appreciate your purchase!

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.130
Just a few more left!

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.210
Ayumu!

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:31.040
Takeru.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:32.420
Sup, Senpai!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.000
Yakisoba, please!

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.630
Thanks! Let me get it for--

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:42.170
What's the deal, Ayumu? I don't need that much.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.290
I'll take all of them.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.290
Oh! Are you sure?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.040
It's what a decent man does.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.960
Oh, and come check out our class's display!

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.290
You sold them all, Senpai.

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:10.170
Yeah! Thanks for your help!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.670
I ate a little too much.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.000
Yeah, why did you eat all that? Are you okay?

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:20.040
I didn't want to wait to see the festival with you.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.750
Okay, then, let's go.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:27.830
Yes, Senpai!

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.210
Where should we go?

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.420
If we're recruiting club members,
we'll want to find a place with lots of people.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.130
That's okay.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.210
Let's go wherever we want.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.210
We don't have to worry about finding club members.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:46.710
You mean...?

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.670
Yes, I'm saying let's go on a date.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.170
Yes! Let's go on a date!

00:13:57.710 --> 00:13:58.880
Not so loud!

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:09.580
A date, huh?

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:10.920
Senpai.

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:11.540
Yes?

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:17.880
I know this whole thing was my idea,
but actually I've never been on a date before.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.330
Is it okay to just act like normal?

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:26.420
Alright, looks like it's up to me.
I'll take the lead on this one.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.040
Follow me. I'll show you how it's done.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:31.040
Thank you, Senpai.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:32.040
Just leave it to me!

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.830
Except that I've never been on
a date before in my life, either!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:40.710
Am... am I going to be okay?

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:47.500
Y-you must be thirsty. I'll buy you a drink!

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.750
What? No, I'd feel bad.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:53.420
It's fine. Especially after you bought all that yakisoba.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.130
Here.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.290
If you insist, I accept.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.630
And I'll buy you a crepe later.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.170
Yes, this pleases me!

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.000
<b>CREPES</b>

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:18.920
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.960
<b>RING</b>

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.960
<b>TOSS</b>

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.210
I'm getting the feeling that I'm actually pulling this off.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.000
Oh! Urushi!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.380
Ooh, you're here, too, Tanaka-kun!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:47.750
Hello.

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:50.580
What's this? Are you two on a date?

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:52.170
Yes, we are on a date.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:52.960
Ooooh!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:58.130
Then I better not bother you. I'll just make myself scarce.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:04.750
Oh, Urushi! Good luck on your first date ever!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.670
First date ever...

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:16.880
Okay, fine! Yes! This is my first date ever!
Is that so wrong!?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.670
Hey! You don't have to be that disappointed about it!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:28.880
No, Senpai. I'm just so happy that I have the honor of
being the one with whom you go on your first date.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.790
Do you mind if I take the lead from now on?

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.170
Yes, I mind! I'm taking the lead today!

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.790
<b>Haunted</b>

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:40.790
<b>House</b>

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:42.330
Sakurako.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.710
Oh! It's you!

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:48.210
I'm Urushi Yaotome, second-year
in the shogi club. Nice to officially meet you.

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.210
I-I'm Sakurako Mikage, first-year.

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.500
That voice... Takeru?

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:01.040
Yeah. He's one of our scarers.

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.960
Maybe we should pass.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.790
Why would you say that? We promised we'd come.

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:06.630
Let's go!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.710
Have a good time!

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:15.750
It's much darker than I expected.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:20.250
It's bad enough that he had
to find out this is my first date.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:24.290
I need to restore some dignity
by showing him I can handle this stuff.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.880
I just wanted to hold your hand.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.540
Is that alright?

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:47.420
I-I guess it's fine, if you want to.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:49.290
Thank you, Senpai.

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.170
Thank you, too.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.420
My next victims should be arriving soon.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.960
Takeru-kun.

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:03.630
Ayumu-kun and his Senpai are here.

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:06.500
Awesome. I'm gonna scare the crap out of--

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:07.210
No, you're not.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.250
You can't go all out on them.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.130
You have to scare them just the right amount.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.080
Aww, but that's no fun.

00:18:16.460 --> 00:18:18.380
We have to help bring them together!

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:20.210
I know, I know.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.790
I'm worried about you,
so I'm going to keep an eye on you.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:37.830
Here they come!

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.500
Just the right amount.

00:18:42.380 --> 00:18:45.540
It's kind of exciting, sitting here in the dark.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:52.540
Senpai!

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:59.080
Takeru-kun...

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.420
It wasn't my fault!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.250
Man, that scared me.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:12.460
Senpai.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.380
Are you alright?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.170
Drink this. It will help you calm down.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:18.750
Oh. Yeah, thanks.

00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:28.460
It's time for a break. We've already seen a lot.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.000
Good idea.

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:32.670
Senpai.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.790
I thought we might want a break
at some point, so I brought this.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.830
Oooh, you're prepared!

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:41.880
Senpai.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.380
What was your favorite part of the festival?

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:45.750
My favorite? Hmm.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.790
It's so hard picking just one.

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:53.250
The crepes were delicious,
and so was the takoyaki and the hot dogs.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.750
And the soccer team's target game was fun.

00:19:56.080 --> 00:19:58.040
So which one was your favorite?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.420
Hmmm, I really can't decide.

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:04.130
And why is it so important, anyway?

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:08.540
I want to use it for future reference,
when I take you on a school festival date next year.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:18.420
Next year, the shogi club will have a display,
so I don't know if we'll have time for a date.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:19.790
Oh yeah.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:24.710
But just in case... if you think of a favorite,
please let me know.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:27.080
Okay, I will.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.040
It's kind of strange, isn't it?

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:45.790
Here we are at the school festival,
sitting on a bench playing shogi.

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.170
Did you not like it?

00:20:48.460 --> 00:20:49.580
No...

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:53.710
My favorite, huh?

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:56.790
I had so much fun, it could all be my favorite.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:01.580
But I think sitting here playing shogi with you,
Tanaka, is my favorite way to relax.

00:21:02.460 --> 00:21:03.460
I see.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:09.540
S-so what was your favorite part, Tanaka?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:13.040
Oh, let me guess! The haunted house! At Takeru's--

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:15.630
What's wrong?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:19.290
Why do you call Takeru by his first name?

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:23.920
Well, that's what you call him,
so I was just following your lead.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:25.420
Oh, is that why.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:26.750
What?

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:30.250
I want you to call me by my first name, too.

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.000
It's not fair for Takeru to be the only one.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:36.750
What?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.290
No... I, uh...

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:39.210
Err...

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.920
O-okay, fine.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.040
A...

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:02.130
Ayu...mu...

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:08.380
D-did I do it wrong?

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:11.250
No... I was too happy again...

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:17.750
I think from now on, whenever you say my name,
I'm going to be wracked with tremors of joy.

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:22.380
Would you please say my name again?

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:24.580
Shut up, Tanaka!

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.040
M-my first name, please?

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:28.250
Not a chance!

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:30.500
I'm calling you Tanaka for the rest of our lives, Tanaka!

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:31.750
No...

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:33.630
Making that face is not going to help!

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:36.330
Then what face will get you to say yes?

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:39.000
None! My answer is no, and no face can change that!

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:04.960
The term "next to" is surprisingly versatile

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:12.000
For example, you can be one meter apart
from someone and still be "next to" them

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:20.080
We're in a stale-mate, in a town dyed rosy red

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:29.000
I want to know your real feelings, but you evade and keep walking

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:38.580
Then I realize we're within 50 centimeters (doo-wop x2)

00:23:38.750 --> 00:23:46.330
Or am I outside of 50 centimeters? (doo-wop x2)

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:53.710
What is the reason we walk home together? (doo-wop x2)

00:23:53.920 --> 00:23:58.000
Unable to ask, our shadows align
